        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
    </selectionEntryGroup>
    </sharedSelectionEntryGroups><sharedRules><rule id="849a-bdda-3647-9ab5" name="True Grit" hidden="false">
      <description>The model may count their bolter as a bolt pistol in close combat and will therefore be allowed to roll an extra Attack dice if they have been equipped with a second pistol or close combat weapon. However, a model using their bolter in this manner cannot receive the attack bonus for charging.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="3f06-9f78-cdb3-abcd" name="Berserk Charge" hidden="false">
      <description>Receive a bonus of +2 attacks when this model charges, instead of the normal +1.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="5531-5dab-d5ba-197d" name="Head-strong" hidden="false">
      <description>The unit must charge if one of their models is within 6" of the enemy, unless the pack is being led by an independent character. They must advance after a defeated enemy, and may never choose to use the optional Voluntary Fall Back rule.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="1b68-7c47-09d6-8f89" name="Wolf Tooth Necklace" hidden="false">
      <description>Models with a Wolf Tooth Necklace always hit on a 3+ in close combat.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="6c08-6890-24c1-ac90" name="Wolf Tail Talisman" hidden="false">
      <description>A model with a talisman is not affected by enemy psychic powers on a D6 roll of 6+. The power still takes effect, but any character that makes their save will be unaffected.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="549f-a32a-cecb-f61e" name="Wolf Pelt" hidden="false">
      <description>A model with a Wolf Pelt receives a +1 Attack bonus when they Counter-Attack.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="64d1-e792-6829-b227" name="Belt of Russ" hidden="false">
      <description>4+ Invulnerable Save</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="7666-138a-d603-3c2c" name="Iron Wolf Amulet" hidden="false">
      <description>4+ Invulnerable Save</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="4e54-2cf9-8614-9bfd" name="Healing Potions &amp; Balms" hidden="false">
      <description>When a Wolf Priest joins a unit, you may ignore the first failed saving throw each turn for the unit. The potions do not work on a model that has suffered Instant Death or that has been hit by a weapon that allows no save.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="f016-3878-b8a5-4237" name="Fang of Morkai" hidden="false">
      <description>At the end of a scenario that uses Victory Points, gain 1 VP per slain Space Wolf as long as the Wolf Priest is alive at the end of the battle.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="d532-2d91-8f4d-deef" name="Wolf Helm of Russ" hidden="false">
      <description>Once per game the relic may be activated to grant all Space Wolves within 2D6" to gain +1 Attack for the rest of the turn. Note it may be activated during the enemy's turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="8728-eb0c-d81c-2553" name="Will Not Teleport" hidden="false">
      <description>Space Wolves in Terminator armour may not deep strike using teleporters.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="1af0-f8ba-01de-6cfa" name="Acute Senses" hidden="false">
      <description>Space Wolf units may re-roll the dice when rolling to see how far a Space Wolves unit can see when fighting at night. You must accept the second result even if it is less than the first one.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="56c7-80f6-57cf-26b9" name="Blood Fued" hidden="false">
      <description>When fighting against marines from the Dark Angels Space Marine Chapter or the Thousand Sons Chaos Space Marine Legion, a Space Wolf will always hit on a roll of 3+, regardless of WS. However, Dark Angels and Thousand Sons will reciprocate and will also hit on a 3+.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="d9e3-41f4-97bd-0202" name="Counter-Attack" hidden="false">
      <description>When charged, unengaged Space Wolf and Fenrisian Wolf models from a unit that has been charged by the enemy must move up to 6" to get into base-to-base contact with the enemy. Treat the counter-attack as you would an assault move, so take terrain into account as normal. Long Fangs may not counter-charge.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="a21d-8086-6b5e-edc1" name="No Matter The Odds" hidden="false">
      <description>Space Wolves ignore the negative Morale check modifiers for being outnumbered in close combat.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="eb08-e222-5bb1-c47d" name="Runic Staff" hidden="false">
      <description>Declare you'll use the Psychic Hood after an opponent has successfully made a Psychic test, but before they have resolved the power. Each player rolls a D6 and adds their respective model's Leadership value. If the Space Marine beats the opposing model's score then the psychic power is nullified and may not be used that turn. Otherwise the power is unaffected. The Hood may be used each time an enemy model uses a power.</description>
    </rule>
  <rule id="46ba-a84f-a9b8-e0a1" name="Move through Cover" hidden="false">
      <description>All members of the 13th Company, with the exception of Fenrisian Wolves and Storm Claw Biker Packs, roll an extra D6 when rolling to move through difficult terrain. Models in Terminator armour, and any packs they lead, do not benefit from this ability.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="8979-e442-986d-39d3" name="Scouts" hidden="false">
      <description>The Space Marines of the 13th Company are adept at catching the enemy unawares. To represent this, the entire army may always be deployed at the start of the battle, even in scenarios where you would normally be required to hold the models in reserve. In addition, after both sides have deployed, but before determining who takes the first turn, all models in the 13th Company may make a "free move," following all the normal movement rules. In this case, Wulfen are not subject to the Animal Rage rule, and a Rune Priest cannot use The Gate. Models in Terminator Armour, and any packs they lead, do not get this free move, and neither do Strom Claw Biker Packs.</description>
    </rule>
  <rule name="Terminator Armour (Space Wolf)" id="db1b-76fc-43b6-9a64" hidden="false">
      <description>Models in Terminator armour gain a 2+ armour save and a 5+ Invulnerable save.


These models gain the Relentless universal special rule. However, they cannot perform a sweeping advance


Space Wolves cannot use the Deep Strike ability normally given to Terminators</description>
    </rule>
  <rule id="decad1e9-1cb7-a7da-0261-4a12948eae91-821f2" name="+1 Damage" page="19" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    </rule>
    <rule id="c497-8813-3ae2-7e77-821f2" name="A Gathering of Ancients" page="47" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>All of the Dreadnoughts from the Ancients of the Fang must be fielded as a single Vehicle Squadron as described in the Warhammer 40K rulebook. However, whilst this formation includes three or more Dreadnoughts, they can all re-roll failed To Hit rolls in close combat.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="9ddeb747-dd42-e0e3-df16-b524ad688ce0-821f2" name="A Glorious Death" page="65" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>Lone Wolf units are never scoring units.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="c5f613c0-a8de-2d4b-3d61-4ef21d2655ca-821f2" name="A Score to Settle" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    </rule>
    <rule id="1fb6b0d1-113c-ac38-2765-e884bc33f7e5-821f2" name="Afterburner" page="154" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    <description>At the start of the turn may choose to forgo shooting that turn. In exchange it may act and be treated like a Zooming Flyer for that turn.</description></rule>
    <rule id="e7631a3f-1fbc-f24c-de42-bb7ace11f322-821f2" name="Agile" page="5" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    <description>A Flyer with this special rule increases any cover saves granted by the Jink special rule by +1.</description></rule>
    <rule id="a08bff8b-c7f3-5c2d-0516-2e866112b074-821f2" name="Agile (Super-heavy)" page="6" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    <description>A Flyer with this special rule increases any cover saves granted by the Jink special rule by +1.</description></rule>
    <rule id="c6b67fde-c965-283f-5447-2261f77ab066-821f2" name="Ancient Tactician" page="57" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>An army that includes Bjorn the Fell-Handed adds +1 to any Seize the Initiative rolls it makes.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="db0f0c32-584c-e438-2f7f-d4e5762597f2-821f2" name="Animal Rage" page="0" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    </rule>
    <rule id="47fc-1bf0-078a-d1ce-821f2" name="Anti-grav Upwash" page="29" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>Whilst this unit includes three Land Speeders, it can move an additional 6" when moving Flat Out.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="5317607a-3f17-ac41-76bc-3552cd4db4a2-821f2" name="Apocalyptic Barrage" page="0" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    </rule>
    <rule id="18e8f256-cd88-b6f0-7b11-5e32df68e8fe-821f2" name="Area Denial" page="153" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    <description>Any successful Morale or Pinning tests caused by a model in this formation on the turn it deploys must be re-rolled.</description></rule>
    <rule id="d1d835f0-140a-48ce-d1d3-324966922435-821f2" name="Armoured Cockpit" page="0" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    <description>One use only; has a 4++ save against missile weapons.</description></rule>
    <rule id="cb2414b0-d17c-0f72-4e5b-396ac68f5ada-821f2" name="Automated Artillery" page="201" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    <description>Unlike standard artillary, Automated Artillery does not require crew in order to function.  It is not removed from play due to the lack of crew and each gun must be destroyed normally before it is removed from play.  Automated Artillery cannot move and cannot charge.  If assaulted they do not pile-in and cannot be locked in combat, their attackers will hit automatically, but must roll To Wound normally.  If a unit of Automated Artillery loses an assault nothing happens, there are no Sweeping Advances, no Pile-ins, and no Consolidation moves.  The Automated Artillery remains in place and may fire normally in future turns.  If the Automated Artillery wins an assault, the enemy must take a Morale test as normal, although the Artillery cannot Consolidate or make a Sweeping Advance.</description></rule>
    <rule id="c6a44270-0d8c-9bd9-f700-f4076257c67e-821f2" name="Automated Repairs" page="54" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    </rule>
    <rule id="421a19b0-8b86-060e-5fc8-b501386a9956-821f2" name="Automated Weapons" page="161" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    <description>Upon landing, each unit within 12" suffers D3 attacks per weapon it's in range of.</description></rule>
    <rule id="f911c47d-1eef-7161-64d9-4f6e706f8e48-821f2" name="Battlesmith" page="62" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description> In each of your Shooting phases, instead of firing his weapons, an Iron Priest can choose to repair a single friendly vehicle that he is in base contact with or embarked upon. To repair a vehicle, roll a D6 and add +1 for each Servitor with a servo-arm in his unit. If the result is a 5 or more, you may either restore a Hull Point lost earlier in the battle, or repair a Weapon Destroyed or Immobilised result suffered earlier in the battle; this is effective immediately.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="f5b77ae8-33e1-d42b-1bc5-aa03ac55f1ae-821f2" name="Beastslayer" page="0" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    </rule>
    <rule id="5d9d410d-2f2d-7ae5-adc2-e0ee25064ac2-821f2" name="Behind Enemy Lines" page="0" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    </rule>
    <rule id="9c285477-1cd5-3589-593c-e51adfbbb208-821f2" name="Berserk Charge" page="0" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    </rule>
    <rule id="22156b8f-7433-3c5b-b5cc-057539a22b0e-821f2" name="Blazing Weapons" page="0" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    <description>Cypher can shoot both of his pistols twice each in his Shooting phase, or can fire them once each either before or after making a Run move.  When making Overwatch shots, Cypher uses his full Ballistic Skill.  In the Assault phase, half of Cypher's close combat attakcs (rounding up) are Strength 4 and AP5, and all remaining attacks are Strength 7 and AP2.</description></rule>
    <rule id="84d6d926-64b0-accb-7d78-1b85870f6940-821f2" name="Blessing of Russ" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>As long as a Dreadnought from this Formation remains within 6" of Bjorn the Fell-Handed, it has a 5+ invulnerable save. </description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="0293-590a-29b9-d274-821f2" name="Blessings of the Iron Wolf" page="47" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>Dreadnoughts from the Ancients of the Fang have the It Will Not Die special rule whilst they are within 6" of their Iron Priest.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="2a4187ea-9b55-4951-6aea-fc41d8c94ba1-821f2" name="Blood Claws Hero" page="59" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>Lukas the Trickster can only join a unit of Blood Claws. If Lukas the Trickster is included in a Detachment that includes at least one unit of Blood Claws, he does not use up a Force Organisation slot.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="1c0d30e3-b4a5-b67c-7c66-126bba7ebf67-821f2" name="Born of Wolves" page="51" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>Canis Wolfborn, and all Fenrisian Wolves and Cyberwolves in his unit, re-roll failed To Hit rolls in close combat during an Assault phase in which they charged into combat.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="dd2b4264-c6fb-66d3-11cc-af4db52f69cb-821f2" name="Burning Retros" page="160" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    <description>?</description></rule>
    <rule id="c0f83592-51f5-3687-c4f2-0101fe82d51a-821f2" name="Caestus Ram" page="144" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    <description>When conducting a ram attack, the player rolls 2D6 and picks the highest number when determining if it has penetraded the target's armour and adds +1 to any rolls on the damage chart. Also confers a 5++ against attacks made to the front armour, including damage from a ram.</description></rule>
    <rule id="41e5-cf38-ca19-c923-821f2" name="Cluster Warhead" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    <description>If the weapon successfully scores a Penetrating hit on a target with an Armour value, roll D3 times on the Vehicle Damage table and select the highest result to apply.</description></rule>
    <rule id="be7ff789-c7cc-ebd2-8063-36b643382380-821f2" name="Conclave of War" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>If deployed as a single unit, all of the models in this Formation lose the Independent Character special rule, though they remain characters. Furthermore, no Independent Characters can join this unit with the exception of Logan Grimnar (unless he is mounted on Stormrider) and Arjac Rockfist. However, the Formation's Fearless special rule is replaced with the Zealot special rule for as long as Logan Grimnar remains with the unit.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="8fce20c7-4989-1f17-1aee-8605459d2a61-821f2" name="Containment Failure" page="0" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    <description>If the main strongpoint suffers a Total Collapse or Detonation! result, roll one dice for each remaining vortex missile.  On a roll of 1-2, the missile explodes.  Place the vortex's blast marker on the center of the main strongpoint, then scatter 2D6"</description></rule>
    <rule id="7b4553a7-eb03-85d1-3ee3-adeb96d2590e-821f2" name="Coordinated Assault" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>As long as at least one model from this Formation is still alive and on the table, the controlling player can re-roll any Reserve Rolls. </description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="2abe74c5-8023-3403-fc39-2536dd449902-821f2" name="Coordinated Attacks" page="0" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    <description>In the Shooting Phase, add 1 to the Ballistic Skill of a Ghostkeel from this Formation if it shoots at a unit that has already been shot at this phase by any other Ghostkeel from this Formation.</description></rule>
    <rule id="7c3519d4-e084-0b4e-8d12-1a0ea3b38564-821f2" name="Counter-attack (Ld 10)" page="19" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    <description>When a unit with this rule is assaulted by the enemy it must take a Leadership test. If the test is successful all models in the unit get the +1 assault bonus to their attacks, exactly as if they too had assaulted that turn.


This rule cannot be used if, when assaulted, the unit was already locked in combat from a previous turn.</description></rule>
    <rule id="8813-a4a2-87e6-3b6f-821f2" name="Counter-charge" page="30" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>At the end of your opponent's Charge sub-phase, you can declare a charge with any unengaged units from this Detachment, so long as each enemy unit that you attempt to charge is locked in combat with another unit from this detachment. Any units that do so count as charging for all rules purposes.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="e60281e5-ed41-0d9d-ea4f-beb543420eaf-821f2" name="Crushing Weight" page="109" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    <description>The Typhon adds +1 to all rolls on the Thunderblitz table when making a Ram or a Tank Shock attack.</description></rule>
    <rule id="c62f740d-756f-c28c-556f-49484634f4c2-821f2" name="Cunning of the Wolf" page="91" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>Before Deployment, roll a D6 for each unit in this Detachment, adding +2 to the result if the unit's Battlefield Role is Troops and it has been joined by an Independent Character from this Detachment (before rolling, inform your opponent which Independent Characters, if any, will start the game joined to which Troops units). On a 6+, that unit has the Outflank special rule. In addition, at the start of each of your turns after the first, you may select one unit from this Detachment that is in Reserves. That unit automatically passes its Reserve Roll to arrive this turn (no dice roll is necessary).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="71b4ae42-3e7b-8a52-747f-401a529dafad-821f2" name="Cunning of the Wolf (formation)" page="91" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>Before Deployment, roll a D6 for each unit in this Formation, adding +2 to the result if the unit's Battlefield Role is Troops and it has been joined by an Independent Character from this Formation (before rolling, inform your opponent which Independent Characters, if any, will start the game joined to which Troops units). On a 6+, that unit has the Outflank special rule. In addition, at the start of each of your turns after the first, you may select one unit from this Formation that is in Reserves. That unit automatically passes its Reserve Roll to arrive this turn (no dice roll is necessary).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="7ceb10d1-1494-e071-f3ad-e939234b83ed-821f2" name="Curse of the Redmaw" page="0" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    </rule>
    <rule id="30d1a6cb-03fb-963e-0005-e164bdb5a00e-821f2" name="Damage" page="0" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    </rule>
    <rule id="2ccdb186-0b32-1955-ff05-50fc392b2c02-821f2" name="Defend to the Last Man" page="0" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    </rule>
    <rule id="75f46c65-7f3d-f7a2-0075-2cbdf9092ce1-821f2" name="Defending Battle Force" hidden="true">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    <description>Once, in each of your turns, you can choose one unit before making any Reserve Rolls. You can choose to pass or fail the Reserve Roll for that unit automatically (it must still arrive on the fourth turn).</description></rule>
    <rule id="979d1cc0-9ed5-22e8-101c-802e25393947-821f2" name="Defensive Strategy" hidden="true">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    <description>If this is your Primary Detachment, you have +1 Stratagem Point to spend when selecting Planetstrike stratagems.</description></rule>
    <rule id="8c5c0d06-bca1-f489-c754-67c455d757a0-821f2" name="Deflagrate" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    <description>After normal attacks by this weapon have been resolved, count the number of unsaved wounds caused on the target unit. Immediately resolve a number of additional automatic hits on the same unit using the weapon's profile equal to the number of unsaved wounds - these can then be saved normally. Models in the targeted unit must still be in range in order for these additional hits to take effect. These additional hits do not themselves inflict more hits!</description></rule>
    <rule id="5cde5c68-b95a-abf8-1343-ad8c0c63efb2-821f2" name="Divine Protection" page="0" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    <description>If there is an enemy model within D6" of Cypher when he loses his last Wound or is otherwise removed as a casualty, then Cypher is assumed to have been captured alive. If there are no enemy models within this range when Cypher is removed as a casualty, then he has made a miraculous escape. If Cypher escapes, then he is not considered to be a casualty for the purposes of awarding Victory Points. If he is captured, then Victory Points are awarded normally.</description></rule>
    <rule id="d4b3d116-b57e-46c1-e3b8-2d6261b65ecb-821f2" name="Drop Pod Assault" page="74" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>Drop Pods and units embarked upon them must be held in Deep Strike Reserves. At the beginning of your first turn, half your Drop Pods (rounding up) automatically arrive from Reserve. The arrival of remaining Drop Pods is rolled for normally.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="f00cf0c4-bb37-10f3-f57b-8c950510c823-821f2" name="Eager to Impress" page="96" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    </rule>
    <rule id="bc49cba4-1a55-5ef4-9052-1d6f8111a776-821f2" name="Explosive Arrival (CoF)" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>During the turn in which they arrive from Reserves, the ranged weapons of all Infantry models from this Formation have the Twin-linked special rule.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="6306218d-9fb8-4ec2-edd5-1a4df8fcf084-821f2" name="Explosive Arrival (HotW)" page="97" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    </rule>
    <rule id="3d07f624-4f87-3389-b892-f6fd53515138-821f2" name="Explosive Demise" page="202" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    <description>When the Rapier loses it last wound, roll a D6. On a 1 you must place a Large Blast on it and all models take a S3 hit.</description></rule>
    <rule id="92ef7076-8fc6-77c9-f977-c6c14a1d8386-821f2" name="Fall Upon the Foe" page="0" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    </rule>
    <rule id="1179ef63-efd4-051e-89a3-3e8dee31b019-821f2" name="Feedback" page="113" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    <description>If a weapon with this type fails its Penetration roll or fails a To Wound roll a D6. On a 1 the firing model loses 1 Hull Point.</description></rule>
    <rule id="f31a9743-91e7-e551-ec6f-c3154bc7637c-821f2" name="Fenrisian Wolves and Cyberwolves" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    </rule>
    <rule id="76df281d-31ad-c62d-e333-9963746616f3-821f2" name="Ferromantic Invulnerability" page="56" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    <description>Ignores Lance and Melta-special rules by attacks made against it. Also reduces the effect of all damage-chart rolls by 1, except for Destroyer Weapons.</description></rule>
    <rule id="0659c2f0-2ade-4c75-631f-ff484780df39-821f2" name="Fighter Ace" page="44" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    <description>d6 Results
1-2 Crack Shot: Fighter Ace has +1BS
3-4 Evasive Manoeuvers: Improves cover save by1 (to a max cover save of 3+)
5-6 Inspiring Aircraft: Fighter Ace and all friendly units within 12" of the model that are the same Faction have Fearless.</description></rule>
    <rule id="fd9a46fc-9ffa-a505-9e99-786705f483bb-821f2" name="Finest Hour" page="0" hidden="true">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    <description>Once per game, at the start of any of their turns, a player may choose to take his Warlord's Finest Hour. The warlord has a 3++ and Eternal Warrior and is allowed to order an All-out Attack. Furthermore you may roll on the Exemplar Tables or use the Sons of the Primarch-rule. These effects last until the Warlord's next turn.</description></rule>
    <rule id="e2a35af3-103c-d845-9205-d4471ba03027-821f2" name="Fire Control" page="0" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    </rule>
    <rule id="51949d39-f57a-d4cb-41a7-1687b23c3f21-821f2" name="Firestorm" page="0" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    </rule>
    <rule id="41121a8b-ffba-09d6-d08a-324b9991b02f-821f2" name="Firing Calibration" page="75" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    <description>May not fire if moved.</description></rule>
    <rule id="db8ad088-19ef-797a-f780-f789a285c39f-821f2" name="Firing Modes - Point Defence, Sentry, Targeting" page="201" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    </rule>
    <rule id="3ba0a003-bc6b-5ccb-2ea5-369a0f4157fa-821f2" name="First Among Equals" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>All Wolf Guard Battle Leaders, Wolf Guard Pack Leaders, Wolf Guard Terminator Leaders and Thunderwolf Cavalry Pack Leaders that are part of a Detachment or Formation presented in this book have the Preferred Enemy (characters) special rule when fighting in a challenge.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="5a54410e-24f9-987a-975f-54519f2a9305-821f2" name="First Among Equals (formation)" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>All Wolf Guard Battle Leaders, Wolf Guard Pack Leaders, Wolf Guard Terminator Leaders and Thunderwolf Cavalry Pack Leaders that are part of a Detachment or Formation presented in this book have the Preferred Enemy (characters) special rule when fighting in a challenge.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="8b2113f1-4b05-bcf0-3f84-5b1caf05c592-821f2" name="First into the Fray" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>On any turn that they disembark from this Formation's Land Raider, the Wolf Guard Terminator unit has the Furious Charge special rule, and can re-roll failed charges.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="ac8c18e9-2874-55a0-0e53-8c77e5e4c4a5-821f2" name="Flank March" page="0" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    </rule>
    <rule id="9b99994b-6dff-a564-e70c-bedb9c5e3124-821f2" name="Flank Speed" page="0" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    <description>If the Cerastus Knight opts to make a Run move rather than firing a weapon in the Shooting phase, it may move 3D6".</description></rule>
    <rule id="308fa059-904b-d984-44a8-52a7eebfae3b-821f2" name="Foehammer" page="0" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    </rule>
    <rule id="f598-bc29-d3c2-0183-821f2" name="For Glory, For Russ!" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>The Wolf Lord, and any units from the Deathpack that are within 12" of him at the start of your Shooting Phase, can either shoot and re-roll to hit rolls of 1, or Run and still be able to charge in the same turn.  Different units can choose different options, so one unit could Run and charge, while another re-rolls hit rolls of 1.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="33c662ba-71c4-144e-e181-3b0534d8f9af-821f2" name="For The Emperor!" page="0" hidden="true">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    <description>If at least half the units in your army have been removed as casualties, you may invoke Divine Intervention. Untill end of turn, all units from the Blood Angel-Faction have Furious Charge and Fearless. Use this power only once per game.</description></rule>
    <rule id="bad2df80-4500-4080-d0aa-289b6867195c-821f2" name="Force Vortex" page="0" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    <description>Warp Charge 4
The Librarius creates a globe of coruscating psychic energy that tears apart the molecular bonds of anything it touches.</description></rule>
    <rule id="c9c5cf35-50b6-169a-f1ae-5d0b3f8742a9-821f2" name="Furious Determination" page="23" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    <description>Whilst Wolf Lord Krom is on the batlefield, all Drakeslayer models have the Furious Charge special rule.</description></rule>
    <rule id="4e687c5a-e4b7-4ca9-159c-3b586f364c49-821f2" name="Graviton Pulse" page="17" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    <description>Instead of rolling To Wound normally with this weapon, any model caught under the Blast template must instead roll equal to or under their Strength score on a D6 or suffer a wound (a roll of 6 always counts as a failure). After the Graviton pulse weapon has been fired, leave the Blast marker in place. This area now counts as both difficult terrain and dangerous terrain for the next player turn, thanks to the graviton flux.</description></rule>
    <rule id="9e0cbe9a-a040-cfdc-25bf-e73966b6e084-821f2" name="Great Wolf" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>As long as Logan Grimnar is alive, all non-vehicle models in this Formation re-roll failed To Hit rolls in close combat.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="3c89b16e-f9f1-c163-550c-76170c16b9a8-821f2" name="Greatest Heroes of the Age" page="0" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    </rule>
    <rule id="51d96645-c10b-66c6-c640-72215c8e560e-821f2" name="Grimnar's Champion" page="70" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>Arjac Rockfist must issue and/or accept a challenge whenever possible. In addition, he re-rolls all failed To Hit rolls when taking part in a challenge.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="51c12063-d44e-ddf7-afd1-44eed03a1edd-821f2" name="Grimnar's Right Hand" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>If this Detachment is your Primary Detachment, you can re-roll the result when rolling on the Champions of Fenris Warlord Traits Table.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="491fce0c-5df2-77aa-2e64-a983d59d1371-821f2" name="Grimnar's Right Hand (formation)" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>If this Formation is your Primary Detachment, you can re-roll the result when rolling on the Champions of Fenris Warlord Traits Table.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="ad79f76b-99ae-5796-8630-a3a137ccdd93-821f2" name="Headstrong" page="0" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    </rule>
    <rule id="0cc4bc7f-eeb5-784c-5884-3024eaf8bada-821f2" name="Heat Seeker" page="0" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    <description>A weapon with this rule can re-roll failed to Hits against Flyers, Fast Skimmers and Super-heavy Flyers.</description></rule>
    <rule id="da4cc1e9-9855-01d0-f968-d551470dce58-821f2" name="Helfrost" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>When a model suffers one or more unsaved Wounds from this weapon, it must pass a separate Strength test for each Wound suffered or be removed from play.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="00225722-c211-36c5-99e3-80953ea8cb40-821f2" name="Howling of the Wolf" page="91" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    </rule>
    <rule id="9bb02d2d-fbaf-c569-f8b1-232db476f152-821f2" name="Hunters" page="0" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    </rule>
    <rule id="879b19d8-744d-fd3a-8402-102d4297c4a8-821f2" name="Hunting Pack" page="97" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    <description>After deployment, but before the first turn, you can nominate one character in the enemy army. All Forgefiends and Maulerfiends from this Formation have the Preferred Enemy special rule against that character. If the nominated character is slain by a vehicle from this Formation, that model regains a Hull Point lost earlier in the battle.</description></rule>
    <rule id="d5aede67-c4da-32a7-b7dd-dff758d8186e-821f2" name="Ice-cold Efficiency" page="0" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    </rule>
    <rule id="a07cd4d4-0388-043a-ba6a-a3ec4b3119aa-821f2" name="If Needs Must" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>When units from this Formation arrive by Deep Strike, you can re-roll the scatter dice if you wish.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="721b6bb8-6e4a-46a7-25e3-a9f9fe9c86d8-821f2" name="Immobile" page="0" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>A Drop Pod cannot move once it has entered play, and counts in all respects as a vehicle that has suffered an Immobilised result that cannot be repaired in any way. This does not cause it to lose a Hull Point.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="bef7ff85-736f-7363-f061-8bd7b092585d-821f2" name="Improved Comms" page="0" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    <description>Add +1 to your Reserve rolls, is not cumulative with other bonuses.</description></rule>
    <rule id="aa46d301-0504-fdf6-227d-374243aad30a-821f2" name="Incredible Reflexes" page="0" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>Ragnar can re-roll a single failed saving throw in each Assault phase.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="902ba875-9ac2-523d-2b77-ba7cdf0a1d7c-821f2" name="Independent Machine Spirits" page="153" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    <description>Deathstorm Drop Pods in this formation may target different enemy units with each of their weapons.</description></rule>
    <rule id="bdf1ab4a-2c0d-cb49-2948-d77b8fd93b73-821f2" name="Independent Turret Fire" page="0" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    <description>As long as the fire raptor has the ability to shoot, each independent turret may fire at a different target and these weapons do not count towards the number of weapons fired.</description></rule>
    <rule id="f4c9c017-7d40-a30b-2a35-36e814f00f42-821f2" name="Inertial Guidance System" page="0" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>If a Drop Pod scatters on top of impassable terrain or another model (friend or foe), reduce the scatter distance by the minimum required in order to avoid the obstacle. If a Drop Pod scatters off the edge of the board, it suffers a Deep Strike Mishap.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="24468216-41b3-b295-3577-bcebb67e2313-821f2" name="Insane Bravado" page="49" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>Ragnar must issue and accept a challenge whenever possible.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="596d8220-53fd-c63e-e0fc-d67cf1cf8977-821f2" name="Invading Battle Force" hidden="true">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    <description>Once, in each of your turns, you can choose one unit before making any Reserve Rolls. You can choose to pass or fail the Reserve Roll for that unit automatically (it must still arrive on the fourth turn).</description></rule>
    <rule id="e4675f80-82d0-040f-4569-d027a34d5fed-821f2" name="Invincible Behemoth" page="66" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    <description>A Super-heavy vehicle is so large and strongly built that weapons which degrade the armour of smaller vehicles will not effect it. Because of this, any attack that says that the target model is destroyed, wrecked, Explodes! or is otherwise removed from play inflicts D3 Hull Points of damage on a Super-heavy vehicle instead.

In addition, any attacks or special abilities that permanently lower the Armour Values of a target vehicle do not affect a Super-heavy vehicle. Note that attacks or abilities that count the Armour Value as being lower, but do not actually change it, work normally.</description></rule>
    <rule id="640900a0-7bf4-dcd9-68e7-879e62f82406-821f2" name="Iron High Priest" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>As long as the Iron Priest is alive, all vehicle models in this Formation have the It Will Not Die special rule.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="fc5f9d0e-0fc5-c70f-7d70-a56c343fa788-821f2" name="Jarl of Russ" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>If this Detachment is chosen as your Primary Detachment, you can re-roll the result when rolling on the Warlord Traits table in Codex: Space Wolves.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="9e22f8fd-6cbf-0ff2-009d-7987408e0091-821f2" name="Jarl of Russ (formation)" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>If this Formation is chosen as your Primary Detachment, you can re-roll the result when rolling on the Warlord Traits table in Codex: Space Wolves.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="1dfa9eb3-b07c-609a-754d-b13555267c17-821f2" name="Killshot" page="0" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    <description>While a unit includes three Predators, they gain Monster Hunter and Tank Hunters.</description></rule>
    <rule id="b4a2-aa20-d4d7-e385-821f2" name="Killshot (Predator Squadron)" page="29" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>Whilst this unit includes three Predators, all Predators in the unit have the Monster Hunter and Tank Hunters special rules.</description>
    </rule>
